DEFAULT_LEGAL = {'terms': {'title': 'Terms of Service', 'version': 1, 'effective_date': 'September 28, 2026', 'last_updated': 'September 28, 2026', 'content': '## AT A GLANCE\n- You must be at least 18 years old to create an account or trade.\n- Only submit gift cards that you lawfully own or are authorized to trade.\n- A displayed rate is not a final payout until the trade is submitted and confirmed for review.\n- Submitted cards may be verified before approval. Approval credits your Bring Gift Card balance; rejection should include a reason where reasonably possible.\n- Withdrawals may require payout-account and identity checks.\n- Fraud, stolen cards, duplicate submissions, account abuse, and attempts to manipulate balances are prohibited.\n- Nothing in these Terms removes consumer rights that cannot legally be excluded.\n\n## 1. AGREEMENT TO THESE TERMS\nThese Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of Bring Gift Card, including our website, web application, mobile applications, account features, gift card trading services, wallet functionality, withdrawals, support services, and related features (together, the "Services").\n\nBy creating an account, submitting a gift card, requesting a withdrawal, or otherwise using an account-required part of the Services, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not create an account or use the trading features.\n\nBring Gift Card is the service and trading name used throughout these Terms. References to "Bring", "Bring Gift Card", "we", "us", or "our" mean the operator of the Bring Gift Card Services. References to "you" or "your" mean the person using the Services.\n\n## 2. WHO MAY USE BRING GIFT CARD\nYou must be at least 18 years old and legally capable of entering into a binding agreement to create an account or trade through Bring Gift Card.\n\nYou may only use the Services where doing so is lawful. We may limit availability by country, market, currency, gift-card brand, payout method, or other operational requirements.\n\n## 3. ACCOUNTS AND ACCOUNT SECURITY\nYou must provide accurate, current, and complete information when creating and maintaining your account. You must not impersonate another person, create an account using stolen information, or knowingly provide false information.\n\nYou are responsible for protecting your password, PIN, verification codes, and devices. Notify Support promptly if you believe your account has been accessed without authorization.\n\nWe may require additional verification before sensitive actions such as changing security settings, recovering an account, linking a payout method, or processing a withdrawal.\n\n## 4. PUBLIC RATES, CALCULATORS, AND INFORMATION\nSome information, including supported gift cards, public rates, market information, and payout estimates, may be available without an account.\n\nPublic rates and calculator results are informational estimates until a trade is submitted and the applicable rate is confirmed in the trade flow. Rates may change because of card type, country, denomination, demand, market conditions, verification results, or other disclosed factors.\n\nWe aim to display rates and material transaction information clearly before you submit a trade.\n\n## 5. GIFT CARD OWNERSHIP\nYou may submit only gift cards that you lawfully own or are legally authorized to trade.\n\nBy submitting a gift card, you represent that the card and any supporting information were lawfully obtained, are authentic to the best of your knowledge, have not knowingly been sold to another party, and are not being submitted as part of fraud, theft, money laundering, or another unlawful activity.\n\nYou must not submit stolen cards, fabricated cards, altered codes, duplicate submissions, or cards you know have already been redeemed unless the relevant trade flow expressly allows disclosure of a partially used card.\n\n## 6. HOW A TRADE WORKS\nA typical trade may require you to select the gift-card brand, country or market, card type, denomination or face value, and quantity. The app may then show the applicable rate and estimated payout before you continue.\n\nDepending on the card, you may be asked to upload a physical card image, enter a digital code, provide a receipt or other purchase evidence, or provide additional information reasonably required for verification.\n\nSubmitting a trade does not mean the trade has been approved. A submitted trade may enter Pending Review or another clearly described review status.\n\n## 7. REVIEW, APPROVAL, AND REJECTION\nWe may verify card validity, balance, authenticity indicators, code status, supporting information, duplicate history, account activity, or other fraud and risk signals before approving a trade.\n\nIf a trade is approved, the approved amount will be credited to your Bring Gift Card balance or otherwise handled according to the payout method shown for that transaction.\n\nA trade may be rejected if, for example, the card is invalid, already redeemed, unsupported, unreadable, duplicated, materially different from the information submitted, suspected of fraud, or cannot reasonably be verified. Where reasonably possible, we will display a rejection reason or status. A rejection does not automatically mean that we are accusing you of fraud.\n\n## 8. RATES AND PAYOUT CALCULATIONS\nGift-card rates may vary by brand, card type, country, denomination, currency, quantity, demand, and market conditions.\n\nThe rate that applies to a trade is the rate confirmed for that trade in the submission flow, subject to verification and correction of an obvious technical or pricing error. If we identify a material pricing error before completion, we may pause the trade and provide updated information before proceeding where reasonably possible.\n\nWe will not intentionally introduce an undisclosed Bring Gift Card fee after you have confirmed a transaction.\n\n## 9. WALLET BALANCE AND LEDGER RECORDS\nYour in-app balance represents amounts credited to your account through approved trades or other legitimate account credits supported by Bring Gift Card.\n\nYou must not attempt to manipulate, duplicate, exploit, or artificially increase your balance. If a verified technical error causes an incorrect credit or debit, we may correct the ledger while preserving an appropriate record of the correction.\n\nUnless expressly stated otherwise, a Bring Gift Card balance is an in-app transaction balance and is not represented as a bank deposit, savings account, or investment product.\n\n## 10. WITHDRAWALS AND PAYOUT ACCOUNTS\nEligible users may request withdrawal of available balance using supported payout methods.\n\nYou are responsible for providing accurate payout information. We may verify payout-account ownership, account names, identity information, transaction history, or other information reasonably required for security and fraud prevention.\n\nWithdrawal statuses may include Pending, Processing, Paid, Rejected, Reversed, Cancelled, or another clearly explained status. Payment timing may be affected by banks, payout providers, compliance review, outages, weekends, public holidays, or circumstances outside our reasonable control.\n\nIf you provide incorrect payout details and we process the payment exactly as instructed, recovery may not always be possible. Where practical, we may assist with a recovery attempt without guaranteeing recovery.\n\n## 11. IDENTITY VERIFICATION (KYC)\nBring Gift Card may require identity verification where reasonably necessary for account security, fraud prevention, payout processing, risk management, or applicable legal obligations.\n\nVerification may include your legal name, date of birth, address, government-issued identification information, identification images, selfie or verification photograph, and related review results.\n\nYou must provide authentic information belonging to you. Submission does not guarantee verification approval. Identity information is handled in accordance with our Privacy Policy.\n\n## 12. FEES, TAXES, AND THIRD-PARTY CHARGES\nAny Bring Gift Card fee that applies to a transaction will be disclosed where required before the relevant transaction is completed.\n\nBanks, payment networks, or payout providers may impose charges outside our direct control. You are responsible for understanding any personal tax obligations that may apply to your transactions. Where law requires us to make a report, deduction, withholding, or disclosure, we may do so.\n\n## 13. CANCELLATIONS, REVERSALS, AND REFUNDS\nA gift-card trade may become irreversible after a card or code has been verified, redeemed, transferred, processed, or otherwise committed through the trade process.\n\nWhere cancellation remains technically and commercially possible, we may allow it. If a transaction is affected by an error attributable to Bring Gift Card, we will investigate and, where appropriate, correct the transaction or provide another remedy consistent with applicable law.\n\nNothing in these Terms removes a cancellation, refund, quality, or other consumer right that cannot lawfully be excluded.\n\n## 14. PROHIBITED ACTIVITIES\nYou must not use the Services to commit or facilitate fraud, theft, money laundering, identity misuse, unauthorized access, abuse of promotions, submission of false documents, duplicate card trading, exploitation of technical defects, manipulation of balances, harassment, or any unlawful activity.\n\nYou must not interfere with platform security, attempt to bypass verification or risk controls, use automated tools to access restricted areas without permission, or access another person\'s account without authorization.\n\n## 15. ACCOUNT RESTRICTIONS, SUSPENSION, AND INVESTIGATIONS\nWe may temporarily restrict an account or transaction where reasonably necessary to investigate suspicious activity, protect users, prevent abuse, secure the platform, comply with law, or respond to a lawful request.\n\nWhere appropriate and legally permitted, we will provide information about the restriction and a way to contact Support. Restricting an account does not automatically cancel legitimate rights to funds that belong to the user.\n\n## 16. CLOSING YOUR ACCOUNT\nYou may request account closure, subject to unresolved trades, outstanding withdrawals, security reviews, disputes, fraud investigations, and legal or regulatory record-retention obligations.\n\nClosing an account does not necessarily require immediate deletion of every record. Personal-data deletion requests are handled under the Privacy Policy and applicable law.\n\n## 17. SERVICE AVAILABILITY AND CHANGES\nWe aim to keep the Services available and reliable, but uninterrupted operation cannot be guaranteed. Maintenance, provider outages, security events, network failures, force majeure events, or other circumstances may temporarily affect availability.\n\nWe may add, remove, suspend, or modify features, supported cards, markets, rates, payout methods, or operational processes. Material changes affecting active users will be communicated where appropriate.\n\n## 18. THIRD-PARTY SERVICES\nBring Gift Card may rely on third-party providers for hosting, databases, storage, authentication, communications, identity verification, payment or payout processing, security, analytics, and other infrastructure.\n\nYour use of a third-party service may also be subject to that provider\'s terms or privacy practices. We remain responsible for our own obligations under applicable law when selecting and using service providers.\n\n## 19. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY\nThe Bring Gift Card name, original software, interface, text, graphics, designs, and other proprietary materials are owned by or licensed to the operator of Bring Gift Card and may not be copied, resold, republished, or commercially exploited without authorization except where law permits.\n\nGift-card brand names, logos, and trademarks belong to their respective owners. Their appearance in Bring Gift Card is used to identify supported cards and does not by itself imply sponsorship or endorsement.\n\n## 20. COMMUNICATIONS\nWe may send messages necessary to operate your account, including security notices, trade updates, withdrawal updates, verification requests, support responses, and important service notices.\n\nWhere we offer optional marketing communications, you may opt out as required by applicable law without disabling essential account messages.\n\n## 21. PRIVACY\nOur Privacy Policy explains how personal information is collected, used, shared, protected, retained, and managed. The Privacy Policy forms part of the legal information governing your use of the Services.\n\n## 22. CONSUMER RIGHTS AND FAIR DEALING\nWe intend these Terms to be read in plain and understandable language. Material rates, fees, transaction conditions, and restrictions should be disclosed before the relevant transaction where required.\n\nNothing in these Terms excludes, limits, or waives a consumer right or business liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, limited, or waived. If applicable law gives you greater protection than these Terms, that law will prevail to the extent of the conflict.\n\n## 23. LIABILITY\nTo the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Bring Gift Card is not responsible for losses caused solely by events outside our reasonable control, incorrect information you supplied, or unlawful use of your account by you.\n\nThis section does not exclude liability for fraud, willful misconduct, negligence where exclusion is prohibited, defective performance where the law provides a remedy, or any other liability that cannot legally be excluded or limited.\n\n## 24. YOUR RESPONSIBILITY FOR UNLAWFUL CONDUCT\nYou may be responsible for losses reasonably caused by your fraud, deliberate misuse of the Services, unlawful conduct, or material breach of these Terms. This does not require you to indemnify Bring Gift Card for matters for which applicable consumer law does not permit such liability to be imposed.\n\n## 25. FORCE MAJEURE\nNeither you nor Bring Gift Card will be treated as having failed to perform an obligation solely because performance was prevented by an event beyond reasonable control, such as a major network outage, natural disaster, war, civil disturbance, government action, widespread telecommunications failure, or similar event, except for obligations that applicable law requires to continue.\n\n## 26. CHANGES TO THESE TERMS\nWe may update these Terms when our Services, technology, risk controls, business operations, or legal obligations change.\n\nThe current version and last-updated date will be displayed. If a change materially affects existing users\' rights or obligations, we may provide notice and request renewed acceptance where appropriate. Minor formatting or clarification changes may not require renewed acceptance.\n\n## 27. DISPUTES AND COMPLAINTS\nIf you have a problem with a trade, withdrawal, account decision, or other Service, contact Help & Support first so we can investigate and try to resolve the issue.\n\nYou remain free to use any complaint, regulatory, mediation, arbitration, or court process available to you under applicable law. We will not require you to waive rights that cannot legally be waived.\n\n## 28. GOVERNING LAW\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria, subject to any mandatory rights that apply to you under another applicable jurisdiction.\n\n## 29. CONTACT US\nFor questions, complaints, legal notices, or support relating to these Terms, use Help & Support inside Bring Gift Card. Additional official contact details may also be displayed in the app or on the Bring Gift Card website.'}, 'privacy': {'title': 'Privacy Policy', 'version': 1, 'effective_date': 'September 28, 2026', 'last_updated': 'September 28, 2026', 'content': '## PRIVACY AT A GLANCE\n- We collect information needed to create and secure accounts, process gift-card trades, manage balances and withdrawals, verify identity where required, prevent fraud, and provide support.\n- Gift-card images, codes, transaction details, payout information, and KYC documents are treated as sensitive transaction or identity information and are not used for unrelated advertising.\n- We may use service providers for hosting, databases, private file storage, authentication, communications, identity verification, security, and payout processing.\n- We do not sell your personal information to advertisers.\n- You may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, object to, or receive a copy of your personal information, subject to applicable law and lawful retention obligations.\n- Bring Gift Card\'s account-based trading services are intended for adults aged 18 or older.\n\n## 1. ABOUT THIS PRIVACY POLICY\nThis Privacy Policy explains how Bring Gift Card ("Bring", "Bring Gift Card", "we", "us", or "our") collects, uses, stores, shares, and protects personal information when you use our website, web application, mobile applications, account features, gift-card trading services, wallet functionality, withdrawals, support channels, and related services (together, the "Services").\n\nBring Gift Card is responsible for deciding how personal information described in this Policy is processed for the Services. You can contact us through Help & Support in the app regarding privacy questions or requests.\n\n## 2. INFORMATION YOU PROVIDE TO US\nThe information we collect depends on how you use Bring Gift Card. You may provide information such as your full name, email address, phone number, country or market, password or authentication information, profile details, and information you send to Support.\n\nYou are responsible for keeping information you provide accurate and up to date.\n\n## 3. GIFT CARD AND TRADE INFORMATION\nWhen you submit or manage a trade, we may process gift-card brand, country or market, card type, denomination or face value, quantity, card image, redemption code, serial number, receipt or proof of purchase where requested, displayed rate, expected payout, verification information, review notes, rejection reasons, and trade status.\n\nGift-card codes and images are treated as confidential transaction information. They are used to process, verify, secure, and investigate the relevant trade and are not intended for unrelated advertising use.\n\n## 4. TRANSACTION, WALLET, AND WITHDRAWAL INFORMATION\nWe may maintain records of approved trades, wallet credits and debits, ledger entries, withdrawal requests, payout status, reversals, corrections, payout-provider references, and related transaction communications.\n\nThese records are used to provide the Services, maintain accurate balances, prevent fraud, investigate disputes, reconcile payments, and comply with applicable legal or accounting obligations.\n\n## 5. PAYOUT AND BANK INFORMATION\nIf you add a payout method or request a withdrawal, we may process information such as account-holder name, bank or payout-provider name, account number or other payout identifier, currency, country, provider reference, and related verification information.\n\nWe use payout information to process withdrawals, verify destination details, prevent fraud, investigate payment issues, and meet applicable compliance requirements. We do not use payout details for unrelated advertising.\n\n## 6. IDENTITY VERIFICATION (KYC) INFORMATION\nWhere identity verification is required, we may process your legal name, date of birth, residential address, identification type, identification number, images of government-issued identification, selfie or verification photograph, verification status, review notes, and related evidence.\n\nKYC information is used for identity verification, account security, fraud prevention, payout review, risk management, and compliance. Access should be limited to authorized personnel and service providers with a legitimate need to process it.\n\n## 7. SOCIAL SIGN-IN AND AUTHENTICATION\nIf you choose to sign in using a supported third-party provider such as Google, we may receive information made available by that provider, such as your name, email address, profile identifier, and profile image, depending on the provider and your settings.\n\nWe use this information to authenticate or link your account. The third-party provider\'s own processing is governed by its privacy policy.\n\n## 8. DEVICE, TECHNICAL, AND SECURITY INFORMATION\nWhen you use the Services, we may automatically process limited technical information such as IP address, browser or app type, operating system, device information, session information, login activity, security events, error logs, request metadata, and feature usage needed for reliability, security, troubleshooting, fraud prevention, or service improvement.\n\nWe may also maintain security records relating to failed login attempts, PIN attempts, session tokens, device sessions, or other account-protection events.\n\n## 9. CAMERA, PHOTO LIBRARY, AND FILE ACCESS\nBring Gift Card may request access to your camera or photo library when you choose to upload a gift card, identification document, selfie, receipt, or other image required by a feature.\n\nWe use files you choose to provide only for the relevant feature, verification, support, security, or legal purpose described at the time of collection or in this Policy. You can manage device permissions through your device settings.\n\n## 10. NOTIFICATIONS AND COMMUNICATIONS\nWe may send in-app or, where enabled, device notifications about trades, withdrawals, account security, verification, support, and important service changes.\n\nOptional promotional messages, if introduced, will be handled separately and with any choice or consent required by applicable law.\n\n## 11. HOW WE USE PERSONAL INFORMATION\nWe use personal information to create and authenticate accounts; operate and secure the Services; display rates and supported cards; process and review gift-card trades; maintain wallet and transaction records; process withdrawals; verify identity where required; provide support; prevent fraud and abuse; troubleshoot errors; improve reliability; communicate service information; comply with legal obligations; and establish, exercise, or defend legal rights.\n\nWe do not use KYC documents, gift-card codes, or bank details for unrelated advertising.\n\n## 12. LAWFUL BASES FOR PROCESSING\nDepending on the purpose and applicable law, we may process personal information because it is necessary to perform a contract with you, comply with a legal obligation, pursue a legitimate interest that does not override your rights, protect vital interests, carry out a task recognized by law, or because you have given valid consent.\n\nWhere processing depends on consent, you may withdraw that consent. Withdrawal does not affect processing that was lawful before withdrawal and does not prevent processing that is supported by another lawful basis.\n\n## 13. WHEN WE SHARE PERSONAL INFORMATION\nWe do not sell your personal information to advertisers.\n\nWe may share personal information with service providers when reasonably necessary to operate Bring Gift Card, including providers of hosting, databases, cloud or private file storage, authentication, email or messaging, security, analytics, identity verification, banking, payout processing, professional advice, and technical support.\n\nWe may also disclose information where reasonably necessary to comply with a valid law, court order, regulatory requirement, or lawful request; to protect users or the Services; to investigate suspected fraud; or to establish, exercise, or defend legal rights.\n\nIf Bring Gift Card undergoes a legitimate merger, acquisition, financing, restructuring, or transfer of business assets, relevant information may be transferred subject to applicable law and appropriate safeguards.\n\n## 14. INTERNATIONAL DATA TRANSFERS\nSome service providers may process information outside Nigeria or outside the country where you live. Where applicable data-protection law requires safeguards for an international transfer, we will use an appropriate lawful transfer mechanism and take reasonable steps to protect the information.\n\n## 15. COOKIES, LOCAL STORAGE, AND SIMILAR TECHNOLOGIES\nThe web version of Bring Gift Card may use cookies, local storage, secure storage, or similar technologies that are necessary for authentication, session management, security, preferences, and basic application functionality.\n\nIf we introduce non-essential advertising or analytics technologies that require consent, we will provide appropriate choices before using them where required by law.\n\n## 16. DATA SECURITY\nWe use reasonable technical and organizational measures appropriate to the nature of the information we process. These may include encryption in transit, password hashing, access controls, authentication, private file storage, logging, security monitoring, database protections, and other safeguards.\n\nNo internet-based service can guarantee absolute security. If we become aware of a personal-data breach that requires notification under applicable law, we will take the steps required by that law.\n\n## 17. DATA RETENTION\nWe keep personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected and for applicable legal, regulatory, fraud-prevention, security, accounting, tax, or dispute-resolution obligations.\n\nDifferent categories of information may have different retention periods. When information is no longer required, we will delete, anonymize, or otherwise securely handle it in accordance with applicable law and our technical capabilities.\n\nBackups may retain information for a limited period before they are overwritten or securely deleted.\n\n## 18. ACCOUNT CLOSURE AND DELETION REQUESTS\nYou may request account closure and, where applicable, deletion of personal information.\n\nA deletion request does not always require immediate deletion of every record. We may retain information where law permits or requires retention, including transaction records, fraud-prevention records, legal claims, security logs, or records necessary to resolve an active dispute.\n\nInformation without an ongoing lawful reason to be retained should be deleted or anonymized.\n\n## 19. YOUR PRIVACY RIGHTS\nSubject to applicable law and lawful limitations, you may have rights to be informed about processing; request access to personal information; correct inaccurate information; object to certain processing; request restriction of processing; request deletion; receive portable information; withdraw consent where consent is the lawful basis; and request human intervention in relation to certain significant automated decisions.\n\nYou may also have the right to make a complaint to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission or another competent privacy authority.\n\nWe may need to verify your identity before fulfilling a privacy request in order to protect your information from unauthorized access or deletion.\n\n## 20. CHILDREN AND AGE RESTRICTIONS\nBring Gift Card\'s account-based trading services are intended for adults aged 18 or older. We do not knowingly permit children under 18 to create trading accounts.\n\nIf we learn that an ineligible minor has provided personal information through an account, we may restrict the account and take reasonable steps to address the information in accordance with applicable law.\n\n## 21. AUTOMATED RISK AND FRAUD TOOLS\nWe may use automated signals or rules to help identify suspicious activity, duplicate submissions, security threats, or unusual transaction patterns.\n\nWhere applicable law gives you rights concerning a decision based solely on automated processing that produces legal or similarly significant effects, we will respect those rights, including any right to request human review where required.\n\n## 22. THIRD-PARTY LINKS AND SERVICES\nThe Services may contain links to third-party websites or services. Their privacy practices are controlled by those third parties, not by Bring Gift Card. Review their privacy information before providing personal information to them.\n\n## 23. CHANGES TO THIS PRIVACY POLICY\nWe may update this Privacy Policy when our Services, providers, technology, or legal obligations change.\n\nThe current version and last-updated date will be displayed. If a change materially affects how we use existing personal information, we will provide appropriate notice and obtain consent where consent is legally required.\n\n## 24. QUESTIONS, REQUESTS, AND COMPLAINTS\nFor privacy questions, access or correction requests, account-deletion requests, or other privacy concerns, use Help & Support inside Bring Gift Card.\n\nIf you believe your privacy rights have not been handled appropriately, you may also have the right to complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission or another competent supervisory authority.'}}

def default_legal(kind: str) -> dict:
    doc = DEFAULT_LEGAL.get(kind)
